# MixAuto Android Car Launcher

Custom HOME launcher for Eonon head units. Jetpack Compose + Material 3, sensor orientation (portrait + landscape), automotive-grade dark UI.

## Stack

- Package: `com.kyuusanq3.mixauto`
- Compose BOM `2024.06.00`, Kotlin `1.9.24`, Compose Compiler `1.5.14`
- Entry: `MainActivity` → `MixAutoTheme` → `DashboardScreen`
- See `AGENTS.md` at repo root for full layout and build instructions
- Kotlin and Compose Compiler versions must stay paired in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
- Dashboard is 100% Compose — do not recreate an XML main layout (`activity_main.xml` was removed)
- Do NOT add `play-services-location` or any `com.google.android.gms` dependency — app targets AOSP head units with no Google Play Services
- App display name **Mix Auto** (`strings.xml`); theme style `Theme.MixAuto`
- Launcher icon: `ic_launcher_background.xml` solid `#000000`, `ic_launcher_foreground.xml` cyan pin `#00E5FF` with white center dot

## UI rules

- Use `MixAutoTheme`; never light mode — head unit is always dark
- Colors: `OledBlack`, `DeepCharcoal`, `DarkSurface`, `ElectricCyan` from `ui/theme/Color.kt`
- Sizes: `CarDimensions` object — min tap target 64dp, primary 84dp
- Text: prefer `CarHeadlineText`, `CarBodyText`, `CarLabelText` from `ui/theme/Type.kt` (ellipsis + maxLines enforced)
- Import theme text composables explicitly when used in dashboard files — a missing `CarLabelText` import in `DashboardScreen.kt` has caused compile failures before

## High-level architecture

```
MainActivity (MapHostViewModel — mapEngine, navigationVoice, localPlaces)
  └── MixAutoTheme
        └── DashboardScreen(mapEngine, mapDataViewModel)
              ├── CarMapViewContainer — map pane
              ├── MediaPlayerPane + ShortcutDock
              ├── PoiDetailDrawer — full-screen overlay when map POI/pin selected
              ├── Lighter-traffic chip in CarMapViewContainer when TomTom alternate qualifies
              └── MapDataOverlay — offline POI / offline map tile downloads
```

- Map: `CarMapEngine` interface in `domain/map/`; swap `MapLibreEngineImpl()` in `MainActivity`/`MapHostViewModel` only
- `LauncherViewModel` — activePanel, poiReturnToSearch, destinationSearchState (rotation-safe UI state)

## LLM architecture invariants

- `MapLibreEngineImpl` is a **facade** — add map/GPS/camera behavior in `data/map/` collaborators (`LocationTrackingController`, `NavigationCameraController`, `MapStyleController`, `RouteRenderer`, etc.); do not grow the facade again
- Edit the **live owner** of constants (controllers / `SmoothingLocationEngine`); duplicate companions in the facade may be stale — grep before changing
- Sample / local-LLM patches: **one concern, one file family**, then compile gate (`BUILD SUCCESSFUL`)
- Soft size: new collaborators prefer **under ~400 lines**; extract only on a clear second responsibility — do **not** blanket-split existing files to a hard 150-line limit
- New `public`/`internal` APIs: prefer explicit return types; skip mass-annotating private helpers
- Package index: root `llms.txt`; map patterns: golden examples in `mix-auto-map-engine.mdc`

## Agent anti-patterns

- Ask-loops ("which component?") — use `AGENTS.md` **Where to edit** table and topic-rule front matter
- Companion-object carpet bombing — change only constants tied to the hypothesis
- Using `RouteRenderer` for puck glide — route greying is not puck smoothing
- Inventing shell syntax or skipping `JAVA_HOME` after a known Gradle failure — follow `mix-auto-build-release.mdc` verify gate
- Diagnosing map label stretch as Compose / `MapHostViewModel` font sizing — map labels are MapLibre symbol layers under tilt, not dashboard Compose text
- Calling `/local-apk` (or publish) while still planning / diagnosing — release only after verified fix (`assembleDebug` gate)
- Retuning `blendDurationForSpeed` or other `SmoothingLocationEngine` companions without a logged hypothesis — use `.opencode/skills/local-map-triage` first

## Shortcut packages (Eonon / AOSP)

- Settings: `com.android.settings`
- Radio: try `com.android.fmradio`, `com.caf.fmradio`, `com.eonon.radio`
- Bluetooth: settings package or `Settings.ACTION_BLUETOOTH_SETTINGS` fallback

## Manifest

- HOME + DEFAULT + LAUNCHER intent-filters on `MainActivity` (Launcher Mode is opt-in via `LauncherModeAlias`)
- `launchMode="singleTask"`, `screenOrientation="sensor"`

## Detailed topic rules

Deep implementation notes are split by subsystem so only the relevant rules load for the file you're editing:

- `.cursor/rules/mix-auto-map-engine.mdc` — camera, GPS/puck, route rendering, style/traffic overlay, custom pins, search origin
- `.cursor/rules/mix-auto-navigation.mdc` — turn-by-turn TTS, reroute, conventional routing, in-nav lighter-traffic alternate
- `.cursor/rules/mix-auto-media.mdc` — media session, album art, audio source picker
- `.cursor/rules/mix-auto-dashboard-ui.mdc` — dashboard layout, shortcut dock, panels, status bar, onboarding, app drawer
- `.cursor/rules/mix-auto-places.mdc` — offline Overture POI database + offline map tile regions
- `.cursor/rules/mix-auto-build-release.mdc` — build, signing, release, emulator GPS tooling
